FamilyTree.person({"id":"anna_haesaerts","name":"Anna Haesaerts","dates":"d. 8 Jan 1880 Bertem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Haesaerts","family":"haesaerts","died":"8 Jan 1880 Bertem","occupation":"landbouwster (farmer)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"jb_coekelberghs","name":"Joannes Baptista Coekelberghs"}],"source":"Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs; Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage","note":"Mother of the bride in her daughter [[coekelberghs]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nnr. 6, 24 April 1873. A *landbouwster* of Bertem, present and consenting, and like her\nhusband [[jb_coekelberghs]] recorded as unable to write or sign.\n\nNamed again in the same daughter's 1903 Kraainem remarriage act, which gives her death:\nBertem, 8 January 1880 — ten months before her husband, and both of them nine years dead\nwhen their son-in-law died at Kraainem.\n\nThe act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date.\n\n`sup`: AGATHA act analyses, not the register images.\n\nFRONTIER — **her forename is unstable across the acts, and it is not settled here.** The\n1838 Bertem marriage, the 1853 birth, the 1873 marriage and the 1903 marriage all write\nher *Anna Haesaerts* plain; two 1867 acts write *Anna Maria Haesaerts*; an 1858 birth\nwrites *Anna Catharina Haesaerts*. One husband, one commune, one occupation and an\nunbroken run of children from 1839 to 1858 make one woman written three ways much the\nlikeliest reading — but it is a reading, not a fact, and the records are deliberately\n**not merged** on it. Only the register images, or her own death act at Bertem in January\n1880, will settle which forename she was baptised with."});
