FamilyTree.person({"id":"anna_maria_bossin","name":"Anna Maria Bossin","dates":"b. 3 Nov 1829 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"3 Nov 1829 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1829-11-03","occupation":"dagloonster (day labourer)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"arnoldus_bossin","mother":"elisabeth_deyn","spouses":[{"id":"franciscus_pardon","name":"Françiscus Pardon","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 Dec 1853"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Sister of [[guilielmus_bossin]], and the first of that generation this tree has besides\nhim. Her marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22) — names her\nparents as [[arnoldus_bossin]] and [[elisabeth_deyn]], exactly as her brother's 1846 act\nnames his, and it is her brother who stands as a witness at her wedding.\n\nShe was of age, born at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 3 November 1829 — a date the act gives to\nthe day — living there still, and working as a *dagloonster*. Like almost everyone in the\nact, she declared herself unable to write.\n\nShe married Françiscus Pardon, a servant of Zaventem. Banns were published in both\ncommunes on 20 and 27 November.\n\n`sup` rather than `doc`: this is AGATHA's transcription of the act, complete as it reads,\nand the register image itself is not linked from the page and has not been pulled."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"anna_norysse","name":"Anna Anastasia Norysse","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Norysse","family":"norysse","sex":"f","branch":"Devriendt","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"mattheus_ramon","name":"Mattheus Ramon"}],"source":"wernero (Werner Osaer)","note":"First wife of [[mattheus_ramon]]. Our line runs through his second,\n[[jacoba_ossaert]], whom he married at Zande on 31 May 1772 and with whom he had ten\nchildren — so no descent here passes through Anna. No dates, parents or children of\nher own are recorded."});
