FamilyTree.person({"id":"arnoldus_bossin","name":"Arnoldus Bossin","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","died":"","occupation":"arbeider (labourer)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"elisabeth_deyn","name":"Elisabeth Deyn"}],"source":"Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans; Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[guilielmus_bossin]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, act nr.\n1, 24 February 1846 (S19), read as an image. The act puts him at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe,\nworking as an *arbeider*, present at the wedding and consenting to it. He signed with a\nmark: the act states he could not write.\n\nThe death entry says only that he was alive on the day of the act. He is nowhere given\nan age, so this record carries no birth date — his son was 21, which places him loosely\nin the 1780s or 1790s and no closer than that.\n\nFRONTIER — his own marriage to [[elisabeth_deyn]], which would name his parents, and\nwhich the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe or Zaventem registers should hold for roughly 1815–1824.\nNeither has been searched for him.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): named again seven years later, as father of the bride in his\ndaughter [[anna_maria_bossin]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853\n(S22). Still at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, present and consenting, still unable to write, and\nhis trade written *daglooner* where the 1846 act had said *arbeider*. The two words say the\nsame thing; the record keeps each act's own.\n\nHe is therefore alive on 1 December 1853, and the death bound moves from 1846 to that date.\nHis known children go from one to two."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"augusta","name":"Augusta Vanstechelman","dates":"14 Mar 1882 Mariakerke – 4 Oct 1922 Mariakerke","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","born":"14 Mar 1882 Mariakerke","order":"1882-03-14","died":"4 Oct 1922 Mariakerke","branch":"Vanstechelman","line":"vanstechelman","father":"petrusjacobus_v","mother":"clementia_w","spouses":[{"id":"petrus_f","name":"Petrus Bundervoet"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950; Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — Augusta Vanstechelman, d. Mariakerke 4 Oct 1922; stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"One of fifteen siblings; her marriage to Petrus Bundervoet is the Vanstechelman–Bundervoet junction.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026). A Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record\ngives birth 14 March 1882 at Mariakerke, death 4 October 1922 at Mariakerke, and spouse\nPetrus Bundervoet — every field as held here, where before this rested on the stechec\ntree alone. Found by harvesting the surname from Open Archives, not by searching for her.\n\nStays `sup`: an index transcription of a card, not an image read.\n\nCORROBORATED FROM CIVIL REGISTRATION (July 2026), not only from a memorial card. Her\nparents [[petrusjacobus_v]] and [[clementia_w]] appear together as the parents on three of\nher siblings' Oostende acts ([[fs-wvl-bs]]) — a couple attested repeatedly in the registers\nrather than asserted once by a tree.\n\nThree of her siblings surface in West-Flemish civil registration, each in an act naming\nboth parents — which is what corroborates the parentage:\n\n- **Henricus Emilius Vanstechelman**, b. 1877, died Oostende 17 January 1941, married\n  Alicia Mathildis St Martin;\n- **Leontius Ivo Vanstechelman**, married at Oostende 20 August 1922 to Lucia Amelia Maene;\n- **Paula Mathilde Vanstechelman**, married at Oostende 11 May 1924 to Alberic Luciaan Delrue.\n\nAll three now have records — [[henricus_e_v]], [[leontius_v]] and [[paula_v]] — at `sup`,\nciting the acts that name them. They were briefly left as a frontier on the grounds that no\nimage had been read, which was the wrong test: adding a person a document names as somebody's\nchild is transcription, not identification, and the rule about two independent identifiers\nguards the second thing. A civil act naming both parents is stronger evidence than the member\ntrees several people here were added from.\n\nHow they were found is worth recording: searching the mother's surname. Vanstechelman is\ncommon at Oostende, Wagebaert is not, so querying the rare maternal name isolates this one\nhousehold out of the parish."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"barbara_debaecke","name":"Barbara Theresia De Baecke","dates":"17 Mar 1709 Oostkamp – 10 Mar 1761 Oostkamp","confidence":"sup","surname":"De Baecke","family":"debaecke","born":"17 Mar 1709 Oostkamp","order":"1709-03-17","died":"10 Mar 1761 Oostkamp","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"rogerius_debaecke","mother":"maria_m_vandewalle","spouses":[{"id":"mauritius_stroobandt","name":"Mauritius Stroobandt","detail":"m. Oostkamp, 30 Apr 1732"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Source detail: Geneanet tree isavdw (Rijksarchief scans; Volkstelling Oostkamp 1748)\n\nWife of Mauritius Stroobandt. Married first Joannes Boeckhout (1729). Parents Rogerius De Baecke x Maria Magdalena Vandewalle."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"barbara_wittenheyns","name":"Barbara Wittenheyns","dates":"b. ~1535","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittenheyns","family":"wittenheyns","born":"~1535","order":"1535","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"petrus_wittenheyns","mother":"judoca_tjonck","spouses":[{"id":"guillielmus_vanrenterghem","name":"Guillielmus Van Renterghem"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Mother of Judocus Van Renterghem. A Wittenheyns of Oostkamp — the same Oostkamp Wittenheyns family that also appears on our Vandewalle line (via Mattheus Wittenheyns ~1500), on a second independent branch."});
