FamilyTree.person({"id":"benoni_rossel","name":"Benoni Joseph Rossel","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Rossel","family":"rossel","sex":"m","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"leontine_schreel","name":"Leontine Schreel"}],"source":"FamilySearch","note":"First husband of [[leontine_schreel]]. `doc`, because the evidence is the same document\nthat carries her: [[edouard_dk]]'s Oostende marriage act of 9 May 1946, read as an image,\nwhich describes his bride as divorced from Benoni Joseph Rossel.\n\nThat is the whole of him. The act names him to establish that Leontine was free to marry,\nnot to say anything about him, so there are no dates, no places and no parents — and\nnothing here justifies inventing any. Neither the wedding nor the divorce is dated in it,\nwhich is why his entry below carries neither.\n\nHe is at the far edge of this tree: the first husband of the second wife of a man who\nmarried into the family. No line of descent runs through him, and none ever will.\nFRONTIER — the Schreel–Rossel marriage and divorce acts, both West-Vlaanderen civil\nregistration, which would date the marriage and give his parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"bernardus","name":"Bernardus Bundervoet","dates":"1837 – 1900 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"1837","order":"1837","died":"1900 Evergem","occupation":"farmer, innkeeper, shopkeeper","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"judocus","mother":"roegiers","spouses":[{"id":"goethals","name":"Marie Eulalie Goethals","detail":"m. 1875"},{"id":"rosalia_dhooge","name":"Rosalia Dhooge","detail":"m. 1881"}],"source":"Geneanet","note":"Widowed in 1879 when his first wife Marie Goethals died — the same year their son Petrus Franciscus was born; he remarried Rosalia Dhooge in 1881. FRONTIER (MyHeritage, July 2026): a record in Belgium, Civil Death Registers 1800-1950 (MyHeritage 21034-1003940) is a death act for him — b. circa 1837, d. 1900 — and it names his father and mother. The values are behind a MyHeritage Data subscription, but as a Belgian civil act the same document should be free via AGATHA or FamilySearch. It would independently test the Judocus x Roegiers parentage recorded here. Member trees also indicate he had more children than the single son Petrus Franciscus we record."});
