FamilyTree.person({"id":"carolus_vb","name":"Carolus Ludovicus Van Bogaert","dates":"2 Feb 1819 Nieuwkerken-Waas – 2 Jun 1892 Sint-Niklaas","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Bogaert","family":"vanbogaert","born":"2 Feb 1819 Nieuwkerken-Waas","order":"1819-02-02","died":"2 Jun 1892 Sint-Niklaas","occupation":"arbeider (labourer)","branch":"Paelinck","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"martinet","name":"Maria Ludovica Martinet","detail":"m. Nieuwkerken-Waas, 1 Feb 1860"}],"source":"Marriage act — Alphonsus Van Bogaert × Rosalia Moerloos, Sint-Niklaas, 7 April 1909; stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"A labourer; father of Maria Magdalena Van Bogaert by his wife Maria Ludovica Martinet (1838–1911).\n\nCORROBORATED FROM A CIVIL ACT (July 2026). He and [[martinet]] are named together as the\nbridegroom's parents in the Sint-Niklaas marriage act of 7 April 1909 ([[S18]]) — seventeen\nyears after his own death, which is ordinary: an act names the parents whether living or not.\n\nThe act also reveals a son, [[alphonsus_vb]], who was not in this tree and is a brother of\n[[magdalena_vb]]."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"catharina_bossin","name":"Catharina Bossin","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","occupation":"huishoudster (housekeeper)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"hendrik_coppens","name":"Hendrik Coppens"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Jan Baptist Coppens × Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas, Kraainem, 27 July 1892","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[jbcoppens]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 4, 27 July 1892\n(S26). A *huishoudster* of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, alive at the wedding.\n\n**Another Bossin of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and again left unconnected.** [[bossin]], the bride's\nmother, is a Bossin of the same commune and the same generation. They may well be sisters or\ncousins. The act does not say so, and this project does not graft on a surname and a village.\n\nNo dates: the act gives her none.\n\nFRONTIER: her own marriage or birth act, which would give her parents and settle whether she\nbelongs to Antonia's family."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"catharina_vanhecke","name":"Catharina van Hecke","dates":"~1620 – ~1670","confidence":"sup","surname":"van Hecke","family":"vanhecke","sex":"f","born":"~1620","order":"1620","died":"~1670","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"livinus_bundervoet","name":"Livinus Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Second wife of [[livinus_bundervoet]], and so a step-mother to [[segerius_bundervoet]] rather\nthan an ancestor of this tree.\n\nWORTH NOTING, NOT CLAIMED: Livinus's son Segerius married [[joanna_vanhecke]] (~1610), and\nLivinus himself married this Catharina van Hecke (~1620) — two van Hecke women marrying father\nand son. In a parish the size of Evergem that suggests one van Hecke family and possibly two\nsisters, but nothing read so far states any relationship between them, so none is recorded."});
