FamilyTree.person({"id":"clementia_w","name":"Clementia Sophia Wagebaert","dates":"1853 – 1927","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wagebaert","family":"wagebaert","born":"1853","order":"1853","died":"1927","branch":"Vanstechelman","line":"vanstechelman","father":"henricus_w","mother":"angela_vd","spouses":[{"id":"petrusjacobus_v","name":"Petrus Jacobus Vanstechelman","detail":"m. Mariakerke, 21 Jan 1875"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950; stechec (Christian Vanstechelman)","note":"Wife of the mason Petrus Jacobus Vanstechelman; died in 1927, the same year as her husband.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026). She is named as the mother — as *Clementia Sophia Wagebaert*, and\nin one act as *Clemence* — on three Oostende civil acts of her children, alongside Petrus\nJacobus ([[fs-wvl-bs]]). Her own dates are still unrecorded here; the acts name her without\ngiving them."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"clementius_robaert","name":"Clementius Robaert","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Robaert","family":"robaert","sex":"m","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"francisca_vanhoutte","name":"Francisca Van Houtte"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Husband of [[francisca_vanhoutte]], who is recorded as his widow — so he died\nbefore she did (17 April 1668, Oostkamp). No dates, parents or children of his own\nare in isavdw.\n\nHer other partner, [[petrus_vandewalle]], is recorded as a partnership rather than a\nmarriage, and their son [[carolus_vandewalle]] was born about 1638. Which of the two\ncame first is not stated anywhere reachable; the order below is the order the\nrecords were written in, and should not be read as a chronology."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"coekelberghs","name":"Maria Theresia Coekelberghs","dates":"22 Nov 1848 Bertem – 1919","confidence":"sup","surname":"Coekelberghs","family":"coekelberghs","born":"22 Nov 1848 Bertem","order":"1848-11-22","died":"1919","occupation":"herbergierster (innkeeper)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"jb_coekelberghs","mother":"anna_haesaerts","spouses":[{"id":"hendrik_vdb","name":"Henricus Augustinus Vandenbemden","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 24 Apr 1873"},{"id":"henricus_vanesch","name":"Henricus Van Esch","detail":"m. Kraainem, 6 Nov 1903"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs; Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage; Geneanet","note":"Source detail: Geneanet; the 1902 Kraainem marriage act of her daughter Joanna\n\nJoanna Vandenbemden's mother; married Henricus Vandenbemden in 1873.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) as the bride's mother in the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]): living at Kraainem,\n*herbergierster*, the occupation already held here. The act makes her the mother of\n[[vandenbemden]] and the wife of [[hendrik_vdb]].\n\nGRAFTED (2026-07-26): her own marriage act — **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6, 24 April 1873** —\nnames her parents as [[jb_coekelberghs]], *landbouwer* of Bertem, and [[anna_haesaerts]],\n*landbouwster* of Bertem, both present and both consenting. It also gives her birth to the\nday, **Bertem, 22 November 1848**, where this record held only the year; her trade at\ntwenty-four, *dienstmeid*; and the commune the marriage was passed in, which neither\nspouse's record carried.\n\nThe link does not rest on her name. Two identifiers already in this tree agree with the\nact exactly: the marriage date 24 April 1873, and her husband's birth — Everberg,\n19 August 1849, to the day. A third bridge pins her across thirty years: her **1903\nKraainem remarriage act** names the same parents again, and names her late first husband\nas *Henricus August Vandenbemden, overleden Kraainem 12/08/1889* — the same death date\n**and** the same commune that the 1902 act established when it corrected this tree's\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe to Kraainem. Three acts, thirty years apart, triangulating.\n\nThat 1903 act also gives her a second marriage this tree did not have, to the widower\n[[henricus_vanesch]], and her parents' deaths: Bertem, 8 January and 19 November 1880.\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`. Nothing about her was refuted — the evidence\ngrew. The demotion is about what the evidence *is*: every act behind this record, [[S5]]\nincluded, is an AGATHA act analysis, the Rijksarchief's own Demogen transcription, and not\none of them has a scan on AGATHA or Open Archives. `doc` means an act or its image was\nread. None was. See docs/research-log.md §51 — this record is one of about twenty carrying\nthe same overstatement, and the sweep is a pass of its own.\n\nFRONTIER — the register image for the 1873 act, which would move this whole cluster to\n`doc`. FamilySearch's microfilm for Sint-Stevens-Woluwe civil registration 1871–1875 is\ndigitised and browsable as DGS **004712751, item 2, images 317–768**; the specific image\nfor act nr. 6 has not been located within it. Her 1919 death is still a Geneanet claim and\nnothing found in this pass touches it."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"coenraets_f","name":"Franciscus Coenraets","dates":"b. 13 Jun 1872 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Coenraets","family":"coenraets","sex":"m","born":"13 Jun 1872 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1872-06-13","occupation":"brouwersgast (brewer's man)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"coenraets_sr","mother":"godts","spouses":[{"id":"henrica_thumas","name":"Henrica Thumas","detail":"m. Kraainem, 15 Apr 1899"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899","note":"Married [[henrica_thumas]] at Kraainem on **15 April 1899** (act nr. 4, S27) — the husband\nher record had been waiting for since the act was found in an index and left unopened.\n\nBorn at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 13 June 1872**, living at Kraainem, and working as a\n*brouwersgast*, a brewer's man — which is worth noting beside a father-in-law who kept an inn.\n\nHe carries his father's name exactly: [[coenraets_sr]] is also Franciscus Coenraets, a\nshopkeeper of Kraainem. His mother [[godts]] had died when he was two.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"coenraets_sr","name":"Franciscus Coenraets","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Coenraets","family":"coenraets","occupation":"winkelier (shopkeeper)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"godts","name":"Anna Amelia Godts"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[coenraets_f]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 4, 15 April\n1899 (S27). A *winkelier*, a shopkeeper, of Kraainem, and alive at the wedding.\n\nFather and son carry the same name in full, which is why the son's record says so explicitly:\ntwo Franciscus Coenraets, one act.\n\nHis wife [[godts]] had been dead twenty-four years by then.\n\nFRONTIER: their marriage, roughly 1865–1872 at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe or Kraainem."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"coleta_b1766","name":"Coleta Bundervoet","dates":"1766 – 1807","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"f","born":"1766","order":"1766","died":"1807","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"petrus_b1727","mother":"marie_anna_dedeckere","source":"paulderidder","note":"One of the eight children of [[petrus_b1727]] and [[marie_anna_dedeckere]]. Their father was\nthe younger brother of [[christoffel]], through whom this tree's line runs, so these eight are\nfirst cousins of [[philippus]]'s generation — blood relatives of Renée and Léon under\nobjective 2.\n\nRecorded from the paulderidder tree's list of the couple's children, which gives the years\nabove and nothing further. No act has been read for Coleta: a birth act at Evergem\nor Assenede would give the day and the parents in the register's own words."});
