FamilyTree.person({"id":"godts","name":"Anna Amelia Godts","dates":"d. 5 Jan 1875 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Godts","family":"godts","died":"5 Jan 1875 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"coenraets_sr","name":"Franciscus Coenraets"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[coenraets_f]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 4, 15 April\n1899 (S27), which gives her death exactly: **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 5 January 1875**. Her son\nwas two and a half.\n\nThe act gives her no age and no occupation, so this record has neither.\n\nA witness at that wedding is **Franciscus Godts**, 54, a plasterer of Kraainem — her surname,\nher commune's neighbour, and the right age to be her brother. He is named here and not\ngrafted: the act calls him a witness and nothing more.\n\nFRONTIER: her 1875 death act, which would give her age and her parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"goethals","name":"Marie Eulalie Goethals","dates":"1842 Evergem – 1879 Evergem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Goethals","family":"goethals","born":"1842 Evergem","order":"1842","died":"1879 Evergem","occupation":"farm woman","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"bernardus","name":"Bernardus Bundervoet","detail":"m. 1875"}],"source":"Geneanet","note":"First wife of Bernardus Bundervoet; died in 1879 — the same year her son Petrus Franciscus was born."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"goossens","name":"Anna Catharina Goossens","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Goossens","family":"goossens","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"vandervarent_j","name":"Joannes van der Varent"}],"source":"Marriage of Petrus van der Varent x Maria Josephina Peremans, Zaventem, 5 November 1840","note":"Named as a parent of the groom in her son [[vandervarent_p]]'s marriage registration —\nZaventem, 5 November 1840 (S29), and nothing more. No age, no dates, no residence in the\nentry, and so none here.\n\nGoossens is a common Brabant surname, which makes her hard to search alone; the pairing with\n*van der Varent* is the handle."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"guilielmus_bossin","name":"Guilielmus Bossin","dates":"1824 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe – 1888","confidence":"doc","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","born":"1824 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1824","died":"1888","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"arnoldus_bossin","mother":"elisabeth_deyn","spouses":[{"id":"peremans","name":"Joanna Catharina Jacoba Peremans","detail":"m. Zaventem, 24 Feb 1846"}],"source":"Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans; Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853; Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 20 June 1872 — Thumas × Bossin (read on AGATHA); Marriage act — Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas × Antonia Bossin, Kraainem, 20 June 1872","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father, by his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of\n20 June 1872, which names the bride's parents as Guilielmus Bossin and Anna Catharina\nPeremans.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named in his daughter's Kraainem marriage act of 20 June 1872 as\n*landbouwer*, living at Kraainem — an occupation this record did not have.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): his own marriage act — Zaventem nr. 1, 24 February 1846 (S19),\nread as an image. He married [[peremans]] there, and the act states he was **born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe**, was **21 years old**, and worked as an *arbeider*. The age puts his\nbirth in 1824 or early 1825, confirming from a civil act the 1824 this record had carried\nfrom a member tree; the birthplace is new, and the *landbouwer* of 1872 was a labourer at\ntwenty-one.\n\nIt also names his parents, [[arnoldus_bossin]] and [[elisabeth_deyn]] of\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe, both present at the wedding, both consenting, and neither able to\nwrite. They are recorded here from this act.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): he appears again as a **witness at his sister's wedding** —\n[[anna_maria_bossin]], Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). The bride's\nparents are named identically to his own, and he is there in person, so this tree gains\nhis sister and he gains a sibling.\n\n**It also dates him twice over.** He is **29** on 1 December 1853, which places his birth\nbetween December 1823 and December 1824; his own act made him **21** on 24 February 1846,\nwhich places it between February 1824 and February 1825. The two windows overlap only in\n**1824, between late February and early December** — two acts, seven years apart, agreeing\non a year this record had been carrying from a member tree alone.\n\nHis trade moves with him: *arbeider* at twenty-one, *steenslager* at twenty-nine,\n*landbouwer* of Kraainem by 1872. He was living at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, where he was born,\nin 1853."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"guilielmus_pardon","name":"Guilielmus Pardon","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Pardon","family":"pardon","died":"","occupation":"daglooner (day labourer)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"maria_anna_pergijsels","name":"Maria Anna Pergijsels"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[franciscus_pardon]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nnr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). A *daglooner* of Winksele, present at the wedding and\nconsenting to it, and recorded as unable to write.\n\nThe act gives him no age, so this record carries no birth date. His son was twenty-three,\nwhich places him loosely in the 1790s or early 1800s and no closer.\n\nThe death entry says only that he was alive on the day of the act.\n\nFRONTIER — his marriage to [[maria_anna_pergijsels]], which the Winksele or Herent\nregisters should hold for roughly 1820–1830, and which would name his own parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"guillaume_joostens","name":"Guillaume Joostens","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Joostens","family":"joostens","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"jeanne_deconninck","name":"Jeanne Marie Deconninck"}],"source":"Death act nr. 35 — Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857 (read on AGATHA); Death act of Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857","note":"Father of Marie Catharina Joostens (1810–1857), who married Georges Thumas — so a direct\nancestor through their son Georges Carolus Josephus.\n\nNamed, with his wife, in his daughter's Grez-Doiceau death act of 10 June 1857. That act is\nthe whole of what is known about him here: no dates, no place, no occupation, because it\ngave none. His daughter's birthplace is recorded there as Woluwe-Saint-Lambert, which is\nwhere this couple were most likely living around 1810, but the act does not say so and it\nis not recorded as a fact about him.\n\nFRONTIER: the Joostens–Deconninck marriage, and his own birth. Woluwe-Saint-Lambert and\nGrez-Doiceau are the two communes to try, roughly 1800–1810 for the marriage.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as the father of the deceased in his daughter's 1857\nGrez-Doiceau death act, read at the archive. He was added to this tree from an index entry a\npass earlier; this is the act behind it. It still gives him no dates, no place and no\noccupation, so none is recorded."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"guillielma_dellaert","name":"Guillielma (Willemijne) Dellaert","dates":"1650 – 1694","confidence":"sup","surname":"Dellaert","family":"dellaert","sex":"f","born":"1650","order":"1650","died":"1694","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"joannes_stockman","name":"Joannes Stockman"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Mother of Livina Stockman (~1688–1744) and so a direct ancestor. Recorded in the\npaulderidder tree with both a Latin form and a vernacular one — Guillielma, called\nWillemijne — in the same style as Joanna \"Janneken\" van Hecke and Joanna \"Janneken\"\nVerbrugghe elsewhere on this line.\n\nShe died in 1694, when Livina would have been about six.\n\nFRONTIER: her parents, and the Stockman–Dellaert marriage."});
