FamilyTree.person({"id":"hendrik_coppens","name":"Hendrik Coppens","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Coppens","family":"coppens","occupation":"metser (mason)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"catharina_bossin","name":"Catharina Bossin"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Jan Baptist Coppens × Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas, Kraainem, 27 July 1892","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[jbcoppens]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 4, 27 July 1892\n(S26). A *metser* of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, the trade his son also followed.\n\nThe act gives him no age and no dates, so this record has none. It does place him alive in\nJuly 1892.\n\nFRONTIER: his marriage to [[catharina_bossin]], which the Sint-Stevens-Woluwe registers should\nhold for roughly 1865–1870 and which would name his own parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"hendrik_vdb","name":"Henricus Augustinus Vandenbemden","dates":"19 Aug 1849 Everberg – 12 Aug 1889 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenbemden","family":"vandenbemden","born":"19 Aug 1849 Everberg","order":"1849-08-19","died":"12 Aug 1889 Kraainem","occupation":"dienstbode (servant)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"jb_vandenbemden","mother":"elisabeth_langes","spouses":[{"id":"coekelberghs","name":"Maria Theresia Coekelberghs","detail":"m. Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 24 Apr 1873"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs; Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage; Geneanet","note":"Source detail: Geneanet; daughter Joanna's 1902 Kraainem marriage act\n\nBorn in Everberg; married Maria Theresia Coekelberghs in 1873; died young (1889) at Kraainem. Named in daughter Joanna's 1902 marriage act.\n\nCORRECTED (July 2026). This record gave his death place as Sint-Stevens-Woluwe.\nthe Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), which names him as the bride's late father, states **Kraainem** — with the death\ndate, 12 August 1889, agreeing exactly. The same man, the wrong commune; the place is now\nas the act has it. He had died thirteen years before his daughter married.\n\nGRAFTED and CORRECTED (2026-07-26): his own marriage act — **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,\n24 April 1873** — names his parents. This record carried them as a Geneanet claim flagged\n*to verify*: \"Joannes Baptista Vandenbemden × Agatha Langa\". The act gives\n[[jb_vandenbemden]] and [[elisabeth_langes]] — so the father was roughly right, the mother\nwas **Elisabeth Agatha**, not Agatha, and the surname was **Langes**, not Langa. The\nGeneanet reading is retired. The act also gives his trade at twenty-three, *dienstbode*,\nand the commune the marriage was passed in.\n\nTwo identifiers carry it beyond the surname: his birth, Everberg 19 August 1849, agreeing\nwith this record to the day, and the marriage date 24 April 1873, likewise. His death —\nKraainem, 12 August 1889 — is then confirmed a *third* time by his widow's 1903 remarriage\nact, which names him as her late husband with that date and that commune.\n\nOnly his mother is recorded as present and consenting. His father is a bare name with no\nresidence, no trade and no consent, which is the register's usual shape for a parent\nalready dead; nothing is recorded from that silence beyond noting it on\n[[jb_vandenbemden]].\n\nDOWNGRADED (2026-07-26) from `doc` to `sup`, for the same reason as [[coekelberghs]]:\nevery act behind this record is an AGATHA act analysis and none of them has a scan. See\ndocs/research-log.md §51.\n\nFRONTIER — his own children beyond [[vandenbemden]]. The held acts name seven further\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe births to this couple between 1873 and 1886, of which two are\ndouble-attested by their own Kraainem marriage acts and are the safe ones to enter next:\n**Felix** (b. 1876-09-10, m. Kraainem 1897-02-08) and **Joannes/Jan** (b. 1880-08-09,\nm. Kraainem 1900-09-17)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"henr_jos_bostin","name":"Henricus Josephus Bostin","dates":"18 Aug 1801 Koekelare – 17 Jul 1867 Varsenare","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bostin","family":"bostin","born":"18 Aug 1801 Koekelare","order":"1801-08-18","died":"17 Jul 1867 Varsenare","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"anna_perquy","name":"Anna Theresia Perquy","detail":"m. Westkerke, 9 May 1833"}],"source":"stefanieschil; Vrijwilligers RAB","note":"FRONTIER above — father of Henricus Josephus Bostyn (1841). Surname Bostin here, Bostyn in the next generation; same family. His own parents not yet recovered."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"henrica_thumas","name":"Henrica Thumas","dates":"b. 24 Jun 1878 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"24 Jun 1878 Kraainem","order":"1878-06-24","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"georges_cj","mother":"bossin","spouses":[{"id":"coenraets_f","name":"Franciscus Coenraets","detail":"m. Kraainem, 15 Apr 1899"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Franciscus Coenraets × Henrica Thumas, Kraainem, 15 April 1899; Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Daughter of [[georges_cj]] and [[bossin]], and so a sister of [[jbgeorgius]] — an aunt of the\nThumas line that runs down to Dorien.\n\nFound in AGATHA's index while searching for her parents' own 1872 marriage: a **Kraainem\nmarriage of 15 April 1899** in which she is the bride and her parents are given as Georgius\nCarolus Josephus Thumas and Antonia Bossin.\n\nACT OPENED (2026-07-26) — the frontier this record named is closed. Kraainem act nr. 4 of 15\nApril 1899 (S27) gives her birth as **Kraainem, 24 June 1878**, her occupation as *zonder\nberoep*, and her husband as **[[coenraets_f]]**, a *brouwersgast* of Kraainem born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe in 1872, son of a shopkeeper of the same name and of [[godts]], who had\ndied in 1875.\n\nThe act also states her mother's death exactly — Kraainem, **7 November 1894** — where\n[[bossin]]'s own record had carried only the year.\n\nShe is one of at least three sisters: [[jcseraphina_t]] married in 1892 and [[misabella_t]] in\n1900, both at Kraainem, both from acts naming the same two parents."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"henricus_bostyn","name":"Henricus Bostyn","dates":"16 Sep 1869 Varsenare – 11 Nov 1947 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bostyn","family":"bostyn","born":"16 Sep 1869 Varsenare","order":"1869-09-16","died":"11 Nov 1947 Oostende","occupation":"metser (mason)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"henricus_j_bostyn","mother":"mathilde_desmet","spouses":[{"id":"judith_cappaert","name":"Judith Marie Cappaert","detail":"m. Oostkamp, 31 Jul 1900"}],"source":"1960dirk (Dirk Teerlinck)","note":"From Varsenare near Bruges; moved to Oostende (died Mariakerkelaan 115). Parents found via the Vynce Lémans (vxnce13) tree — his direct ancestry, sourced to the Rijksarchief."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"henricus_e_v","name":"Henricus Emilius Vanstechelman","dates":"1877 – 17 Jan 1941 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","sex":"m","born":"1877","order":"1877","died":"17 Jan 1941 Oostende","branch":"Vanstechelman","line":"vanstechelman","father":"petrusjacobus_v","mother":"clementia_w","spouses":[{"id":"alicia_stmartin","name":"Alicia Mathildis St Martin"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950","note":"Elder brother of [[augusta]], and so a brother-in-law of Petrus Franciscus Bundervoet.\n\nFrom his own Oostende death registration of 17 January 1941, which names his parents as\nPetrus Jacobus and Clemencia Sophia Wagebaert and his wife as Alicia Mathildis St Martin.\nThe birth year of 1877 is the one the death act implies rather than a stated date, so it is\nrecorded as a bare year.\n\nThe act is an index entry and has not been read as an image, which is why this stays `sup`.\nHis wife has no record of her own yet."});
