FamilyTree.person({"id":"henricus_vanesch","name":"Henricus Van Esch","dates":"b. 23 Nov 1836 Bertem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Esch","family":"vanesch","born":"23 Nov 1836 Bertem","order":"1836-11-23","occupation":"herbergier (innkeeper)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"coekelberghs","name":"Maria Theresia Coekelberghs","detail":"m. Kraainem, 6 Nov 1903"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage","note":"[[coekelberghs]]'s second husband, married at Kraainem on 6 November 1903 (act nr. 16) —\nfourteen years after she was widowed of [[hendrik_vdb]], and he a widower himself.\n\nBorn at Bertem on 23 November 1836, which is her own birth commune, and an *herbergier* at\nZaventem, which is her own trade: she is recorded as *herbergierster* on her daughter's\n1902 marriage act. Two innkeepers from the same village, marrying in their sixties.\n\nHe marries into this tree rather than descending in it: nothing here claims a blood\nrelation, and he is recorded because the act that names him is the same act that gives\n[[jb_coekelberghs]] and [[anna_haesaerts]] their death dates.\n\n`sup`: an AGATHA act analysis (Demogen project huvlb20), not the register image. Beware the\nOpen Archives mirror of this act — its rendered HTML gives all three death dates one day\nearlier than both its own API record and the AGATHA page.\n\nFRONTIER — his first marriage and his parents, neither read. A widower of Bertem born in\n1836 should have both a first marriage and a first wife's death in the Bertem or Zaventem\nregisters."});
