FamilyTree.person({"id":"janbaptist_p","name":"Jan Baptist Paelinck","dates":"20 May 1771 Destelbergen – 29 May 1843 Lokeren","confidence":"sup","surname":"Paelinck","family":"paelinck","born":"20 May 1771 Destelbergen","order":"1771-05-20","died":"29 May 1843 Lokeren","occupation":"dagloner (day labourer)","branch":"Paelinck","line":"paelinck","father":"apolonius_p","mother":"christina_vm","spouses":[{"id":"joanna_va","name":"Joanna Coleta Van Acker","detail":"m. 1795"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"A day labourer; the family moved from Destelbergen to Lokeren, where he died. His wife was Joanna Coleta Van Acker."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jb_coekelberghs","name":"Joannes Baptista Coekelberghs","dates":"d. 19 Nov 1880 Bertem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Coekelberghs","family":"coekelberghs","died":"19 Nov 1880 Bertem","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"anna_haesaerts","name":"Anna Haesaerts"}],"source":"Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs; Kraainem marriage act nr. 16, 6 November 1903 — Van Esch × Coekelberghs, her remarriage","note":"Father of the bride in his daughter [[coekelberghs]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nnr. 6, 24 April 1873. A *landbouwer* of Bertem, present at the wedding and consenting to\nit, and recorded as unable to write or sign, *ongeletterd zijnde*.\n\nNamed a second time, thirty years later, in the same daughter's remarriage act — Kraainem\nnr. 16, 6 November 1903 — which is where his death comes from: Bertem, 19 November 1880.\nTwo acts three decades apart naming the same man as her father is what carries this link;\nthe 1873 act alone would be a surname and a commune.\n\n`sup` rather than `doc`: both are AGATHA act analyses — the Rijksarchief's own Demogen\ntranscriptions — and neither act has a scan on AGATHA or Open Archives.\n\nFRONTIER — his own marriage, which the registry already holds as\n`bertem-1838-marriage-coeckelberghs-haesaerts`: Bertem nr. 8, 30 October 1838, giving him\nas born at Bertem 29 July 1809, a *slagter*, son of *Henricus Coeckelberghs* and\n*Petronella Elseviers*. It is not grafted here for two reasons. The act is unread beyond\nits transcription, and the trade moves — *slagter* in 1838, 1853 and 1867, *landbouwer* in\n1858, 1861 and 1873 — while the wife's forename is written three ways across the same\nspan (see [[anna_haesaerts]]). One man recorded loosely over forty-five years is much the\nlikeliest reading, but *Joannes Baptista Coekelberghs* is a common enough name in Brabant\nthat several distinct men carry it between 1793 and 1921, so the birth and the generation\nabove wait for the register image. That image exists and is reachable:\n`https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:9392-HGZ1-T?i=217&cc=1482191&cat=140936`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jb_vandenbemden","name":"Jan Baptist Van den Bemden","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van den Bemden","family":"vandenbemden","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"elisabeth_langes","name":"Elisabeth Agatha Langes"}],"source":"Sint-Stevens-Woluwe marriage act nr. 6, 24 April 1873 — Van den Bemden × Coekelberghs","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[hendrik_vdb]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe nr. 6,\n24 April 1873.\n\n**What the act does not say about him is the informative part.** His wife\n[[elisabeth_langes]] is given a residence, a trade and the words *present and consenting*;\nhe is given a name and nothing else — no commune, no occupation, no consent. That is the\nregister's usual shape for a parent already dead, and it is why this record carries no\ndeath entry at all rather than a `raw` note claiming he was alive: a bare name is not a\nstatement either way, and inventing \"alive on 24 April 1873\" from silence would be exactly\nthe guess the grammar has no syntax for.\n\nHe confirms — and corrects — an unverified Geneanet claim this tree had been carrying on\nhis son's record, which named him *Joannes Baptista Vandenbemden*. The act's own spelling\nis *Jan Baptist Van den Bemden*, and it is followed here.\n\n`sup`: an AGATHA act analysis, not the register image.\n\nFRONTIER — his own marriage to Elisabeth Agatha Langes, which the Everberg or Kortenberg\nregisters should hold for roughly 1840–1849 and which would name his parents; and his\ndeath, which on the reading above falls before April 1873. Two Van den Bemden witnesses\nstood at his son's wedding — *Lodewijk*, 40, daglooner of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, and\n*Willem*, 26, landbouwer of Schaarbeek — and one of them is likely his son or his brother.\nNeither is grafted: the act states no kinship for either."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jbbossin","name":"Joannes Baptista Bossin","dates":"d. 19 Mar 1887 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bossin","family":"bossin","died":"19 Mar 1887 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"maria_wolf","name":"Maria Wolf"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900","note":"Father of the groom in his son [[ludovicus_bossin79]]'s marriage act — Kraainem nr. 3, 10\nApril 1900 (S28), which gives his death as **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 19 March 1887**. His son was\nseven.\n\nThe act gives him no age and no trade, so this record has neither.\n\n**Whether he belongs to [[bossin]]'s family is the open question of this act** — the same\nsurname, the same small commune, the same generation. It is not answered here and not assumed.\n\nFRONTIER: his 1887 death act and his marriage to [[maria_wolf]], either of which would name\nhis parents and settle it."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jbcoppens","name":"Jan Baptist Coppens","dates":"b. 6 Mar 1870 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Coppens","family":"coppens","sex":"m","born":"6 Mar 1870 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1870-03-06","occupation":"metser (mason)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"hendrik_coppens","mother":"catharina_bossin","spouses":[{"id":"jcseraphina_t","name":"Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas","detail":"m. Kraainem, 27 Jul 1892"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Jan Baptist Coppens × Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas, Kraainem, 27 July 1892","note":"Married [[jcseraphina_t]] at Kraainem on **27 July 1892** (act nr. 4, S26). Born at\nSint-Stevens-Woluwe on **6 March 1870**, a *metser* like his father [[hendrik_coppens]], and\nliving in his birth commune when he married.\n\nHe turns up again in his sisters-in-law's weddings — a witness, aged 29, at [[henrica_thumas]]'s\nin 1899 and, aged 30, at [[misabella_t]]'s in 1900. The families stayed close.\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jbgeorgius","name":"Joannes Baptista Georgius Thumas","dates":"26 Sep 1876 Kraainem – 23 Mar 1944 Brussel","confidence":"doc","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"26 Sep 1876 Kraainem","order":"1876-09-26","died":"23 Mar 1944 Brussel","occupation":"fabriekwerker & gemeenteschepen (factory worker & alderman)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"georges_cj","mother":"bossin","spouses":[{"id":"vandenbemden","name":"Joanna Vandenbemden","detail":"m. Kraainem, 3 Feb 1902"}],"source":"Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 3 February 1902 — Thumas × Vandenbemden; marcelcroon (Marcel Croon); jswaelens","note":"Son of Georges Carolus Josephus and Antoina Bossin. A factory worker who also served as a schepen (municipal alderman) in Kraainem. Married Joanna Vandenbemden in Kraainem on 3 Feb 1902.\n\nDOCUMENTED (July 2026) by the Kraainem marriage act of 3 February 1902 (akte nr. 2, [[S5]]), where he is the bridegroom. It gives his birth at\nKraainem on 26 September 1876 and his trade as *fabriekwerker*, both as held here, and\nnames his parents outright — Georgius Carolus Josephus Thumas and Antonia Bossin. He was\nliving at Sint-Stevens-Woluwe when he married. The alderman's office in his occupation\nfield came from elsewhere and is not in this act."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jbzenon_t","name":"Jean Baptiste Zénon Thumas","dates":"b. Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"Grez-Doiceau","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"georges2_t","mother":"joostens","source":"The children of Georges Thumas x Marie Catherine Joostens at Grez-Doiceau, 1835-1868","note":"Younger brother of [[georges_cj]]. His birth was declared at Grez-Doiceau on **20 August\n1845** (S25), between his brother [[georgesjoseph_t]] in 1843 and [[charleseugene_t]] in 1850.\n\n`raw` rather than a date: the index gives the declaration, not the birth.\n\n`sup`: an index row, no register image read.\n\nFRONTIER: his birth act, and whether he lived to marry — nothing is known of him after 1845.\n*Zénon* is an unusual enough forename to search on its own, which is worth trying before the\ncommon ones."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jcseraphina_t","name":"Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas","dates":"b. 21 Mar 1873 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"21 Mar 1873 Kraainem","order":"1873-03-21","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"georges_cj","mother":"bossin","spouses":[{"id":"jbcoppens","name":"Jan Baptist Coppens","detail":"m. Kraainem, 27 Jul 1892"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 4 — Jan Baptist Coppens × Joanna Catharina Seraphina Thumas, Kraainem, 27 July 1892","note":"Eldest known child of [[georges_cj]] and [[bossin]] — born at **Kraainem on 21 March 1873**,\nnine months after her parents married there in June 1872, and so the first of the Kraainem\ngeneration.\n\nHer marriage act (Kraainem nr. 4, 27 July 1892, S26) gives her *zonder beroep* and names both\nparents: her father a *fabriekbediende*, her mother [[bossin]] still living and keeping house.\nHer mother would be dead two years later.\n\nShe married **Jan Baptist Coppens**, a mason of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe.\n\n`sup`: AGATHA's transcription of the act, complete as it reads, but the register image has not\nbeen pulled."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jean_t","name":"Jean Thumas","dates":"23 Oct 1907 Kraainem – 22 Mar 1995 Kraainem","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"23 Oct 1907 Kraainem","order":"1907-10-23","died":"22 Mar 1995 Kraainem","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"jbgeorgius","mother":"vandenbemden","spouses":[{"id":"crabbe","name":"Marie Louise Crabbé"}],"note":"DOCUMENTED (b. 23 Oct 1907, d. 22 Mar 1995, both in Kraainem; Geneanet, marcelcroon). He lived his whole life in Kraainem and is the strongly-supported grandfather of Thiery. The ONE remaining sealed link is Jean → François (Thiery’s father), whose 20th-century birth is behind the 100-year civil-registration privacy wall."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jeanlambert_t","name":"Jean Lambert Thumas","dates":"26 Sep 1701 Grez-Doiceau – 3 Mar 1776 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"doc","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","born":"26 Sep 1701 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1701-09-26","died":"3 Mar 1776 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"marguillier & greffier (church warden / parish clerk)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"antoine_t","mother":"daix","spouses":[{"id":"leclercq_t","name":"Marie Jacqueline Leclercq","detail":"m. Wavre, 23 Feb 1743"}],"source":"Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; m2155","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a father. His son Georges's death act (Grez-Doiceau, 20\nNovember 1808) names the dead man's father as *Lambert Thumas* and his mother as Marie\nLeclercq — the pairing this record already asserts, now on a civil act rather than on the\nm2155 tree alone. The act gives the short form of his name, without the *Jean*.\n\nChurch warden and parish clerk of Grez-Doiceau. Our line descends from his SECOND marriage, to Marie Jacqueline Leclercq (Wavre, 1743) — their son Georges (1744) continues the line. His first wife was Marie Catherine Crèvecœur (m. 1727, d. 1742).\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as *Lambert Thumas of Grez*, father of the deceased, in his son\nGeorge's 1808 Grez-Doiceau death act — with [[leclercq_t]] as the mother. The couple and the\nparentage are now on a civil act."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jeanne_deconninck","name":"Jeanne Marie Deconninck","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Deconninck","family":"deconninck","sex":"f","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"guillaume_joostens","name":"Guillaume Joostens"}],"source":"Death act nr. 35 — Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857 (read on AGATHA); Death act of Marie Catherine Joostens, Grez-Doiceau, 10 June 1857","note":"Mother of Marie Catharina Joostens (1810–1857) and so a direct ancestor.\n\nNamed alongside her husband in her daughter's Grez-Doiceau death act of 10 June 1857, which\nis the only source read for her. It gives her no dates and no place; none is invented here.\n\nThe surname is Flemish (De Coninck / Deconinck are the commoner spellings) in a\nWalloon-Brabant setting, which is worth noting for the search: the family may have come to\nWoluwe-Saint-Lambert or Grez-Doiceau from Flanders, and the name may be spelled either way\nin the registers.\n\nFRONTIER: the Joostens–Deconninck marriage, and her own parents.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as the mother of the deceased in her daughter's 1857\nGrez-Doiceau death act, read at the archive. As with her husband, the act gives her nothing\nbeyond the name."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"jerome_dk","name":"Jerome Joseph Dekeyser","dates":"14 Jun 1897 Oostende – 1972 Oostende","confidence":"doc","surname":"Dekeyser","family":"dekeyser","born":"14 Jun 1897 Oostende","order":"1897-06-14","died":"1972 Oostende","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","father":"edouard_dk","mother":"louise_bocklandt","spouses":[{"id":"leonie_p","name":"Léonie (Philomena Leonia) Paelinck","detail":"m. Sint-Niklaas, 10 Dec 1919"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck); Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Source detail: Stef Paelinck (stefpaelinck) tree; Oostende Burgerzaken; Rijksarchief AGATHA (Oostende birth act nr. 585, 1897)\n\nCONFIRMED Roland's grandfather (Cosette). Full first names Jérôme Josephus; born Oostende 14 Jun 1897 (birth act nr. 585, Rijksarchief AGATHA). Born before his parents married: he was LEGITIMIZED by their marriage on 4 May 1901 (marginal note 'Gewettigd 4 5 1901' on his birth act). Lived in Oostende (Blauwkasteelstraat 21; later Amsterdamstraat 38). Recorded child: Albert Dekeyser (1920–1972); Gustaaf (Roland's father) is another of their sons. His siblings (children of Édouard × Louise, per AGATHA): Gustavus Josephus (1899, also legitimized 1901), Bertha Alida Theresia (1901), Maria (1902–2002), Angela Luciana (†1903) and Cesar Mauritius (†1905) — the last two died in infancy."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"joanna_b1761","name":"Joanna Bundervoet","dates":"1761 – 1825","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"f","born":"1761","order":"1761","died":"1825","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"petrus_b1727","mother":"marie_anna_dedeckere","source":"paulderidder","note":"One of the eight children of [[petrus_b1727]] and [[marie_anna_dedeckere]]. Their father was\nthe younger brother of [[christoffel]], through whom this tree's line runs, so these eight are\nfirst cousins of [[philippus]]'s generation — blood relatives of Renée and Léon under\nobjective 2.\n\nRecorded from the paulderidder tree's list of the couple's children, which gives the years\nabove and nothing further. No act has been read for Joanna: a birth act at Evergem\nor Assenede would give the day and the parents in the register's own words."});
