FamilyTree.person({"id":"joanna_verbrugghe","name":"Joanna (Janneken) Verbrugghe","dates":"~1655 – 1704","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verbrugghe","family":"verbrugghe","born":"~1655","order":"1655","died":"1704","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"nicolas_verbrugghe","spouses":[{"id":"joannes_b1637","name":"Joannes Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Mother of Joannes Bundervoet (~1682).\n\nCORRECTED (July 2026): this record said \"her own parents not recorded here\". They are —\nthe paulderidder ancestry chart names her father as Nicolas Verbrugghe, now linked. Her\nmother is shown there only as \"?\", so that side is still open.\n\nNote the near-miss: this tree holds another Joanna Verbrugghe, who died at Hontenisse in\n1734, married Petrus van Huffel, and was a daughter of Gerard Verbrugge x Anna de Cock.\nShe is a different woman. A Geneanet URL without an occurrence number lands on her\nfirst, so anyone re-checking this line should follow the link from Joannes Bundervoet's\nprofile rather than searching the name."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"joanna_verelst","name":"Joanna Theresia Ver Elst","dates":"d. 19 Dec 1843 Zaventem","confidence":"doc","surname":"Ver Elst","family":"verelst","died":"19 Dec 1843 Zaventem","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"egidius_peremans","name":"Egidius Peremans"}],"source":"Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans","note":"Mother of the bride in her daughter [[peremans]]'s marriage act — Zaventem, act nr. 1,\n24 February 1846 (S19), read as an image. She was dead by then, at Zaventem on 19 December\n1843, six years after her husband [[egidius_peremans]] and barely two years before her\ndaughter married.\n\nThe act gives her no age and no occupation, so this record has neither.\n\nThe surname is written *Ver Elst* on the act, in two words. Verelst and Van Elst are the\nusual Brabant forms, and her own acts will show which the family wrote.\n\nFRONTIER — her 1843 Zaventem death act, which should give her age and her parents. Note\nthat her daughter declared to the 1846 act, with her witnesses, that she had never known\nher grandparents nor where they died: this generation was not reachable through the\nfamily's own memory in 1846, and it will have to come from the registers."});
