FamilyTree.person({"id":"joannes_vi","name":"Joannes Van Iseghem","dates":"11 May 1903 Lens (Fr) – 5 May 1969 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Iseghem","family":"vaniseghem","born":"11 May 1903 Lens (Fr)","order":"1903-05-11","died":"5 May 1969 Oostende","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"van-iseghem","father":"eduardus_vi","mother":"emma_vincke","spouses":[{"id":"adrienne_dv","name":"Adrienne Margaretha Devriendt"}],"source":"Memorial card — Joannes Vaniseghem, d. Oostende 5 May 1969; bartvanhooren (Bart Vanhooren); gverdievel (Guy Verdievel)","note":"Born in the French coal-mining town of Lens, where his Oostende family had emigrated for work; the family later returned to Belgium. Died six days short of his 66th birthday.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026) by a Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial-card record:\nborn **Lens** 11 May 1903, died Oostende 5 May 1969, partner Adrienne Devriendt. The\nbirthplace is the striking part — an Oostende family with a son born at Lens — and the\ncard gives it independently of the trees, which is the strongest single reason to believe\nthis is the same man. This record notes Lens as being in France; the card says only\n\"Lens\", so which Lens is not settled here."});
