FamilyTree.person({"id":"maria_anna_pergijsels","name":"Maria Anna Pergijsels","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Pergijsels","family":"pergijsels","died":"","occupation":"dagloonster (day labourer)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"guilielmus_pardon","name":"Guilielmus Pardon"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 9 — Françiscus Pardon × Anna Maria Bossin, Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, 1 December 1853","note":"Mother of the groom in her son [[franciscus_pardon]]'s marriage act — Sint-Stevens-Woluwe\nnr. 9, 1 December 1853 (S22). A *dagloonster* of Winksele, present and consenting, and\nlike her husband [[guilielmus_pardon]] recorded as unable to write.\n\nThe act gives her no age, so this record carries no birth date, and the death entry says\nonly that she was alive on the day.\n\nThe surname is a rare one and its spelling is unsettled — *Pergijsels* is what the act\nwrites, and Pergijssels, Pergisels and Peregijsels all occur in Brabant. That rarity is\nworth more than it looks: a surname this uncommon is exactly the kind that can be searched\non its own, where Bossin and Pardon cannot."});
