FamilyTree.person({"id":"misabella_t","name":"Maria Isabella Helena Thumas","dates":"b. 18 Aug 1880 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"18 Aug 1880 Sint-Stevens-Woluwe","order":"1880-08-18","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"georges_cj","mother":"bossin","spouses":[{"id":"ludovicus_bossin79","name":"Ludovicus Bossin","detail":"m. Kraainem, 10 Apr 1900"}],"source":"Marriage act nr. 3 — Ludovicus Bossin × Maria Isabella Helena Thumas, Kraainem, 10 April 1900","note":"Daughter of [[georges_cj]] and [[bossin]], born at **Sint-Stevens-Woluwe on 18 August 1880**\n— the family had moved on from Kraainem, where her sisters were born, and her birth was\ndeclared on the 26th, which is the entry AGATHA carries separately under her mother's name.\n\nAt nineteen she was a *dienstmeid*, a housemaid, living at Kraainem. She married **Ludovicus\nBossin**, a polisher of Sint-Stevens-Woluwe, on **10 April 1900** (Kraainem act nr. 3, S28).\nHer mother had been dead five years by then; the act records it.\n\n**Her husband's surname is her mother's.** Whether the two Bossin families are one is not\nestablished here and is not assumed — see [[ludovicus_bossin79]].\n\n`sup`: an act analysis, not the register image."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"mjosephina_peremans","name":"Maria Josephina Peremans","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Peremans","family":"peremans","sex":"f","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"egidius_peremans","mother":"joanna_verelst","spouses":[{"id":"vandervarent_p","name":"Petrús van der Varent","detail":"m. Zaventem, 5 Nov 1840"}],"source":"Marriage of Petrus van der Varent x Maria Josephina Peremans, Zaventem, 5 November 1840","note":"The first sibling this tree has for [[peremans]]. She married **Petrús van der Varent** at\n**Zaventem on 5 November 1840** (S29), her parents given as [[egidius_peremans]] and\n[[joanna_verelst]] — the same pair, with the same distinctive three-part maternal name, that\nher sister's 1846 act gives.\n\nHer father had been dead three and a half years by then; her mother had three years to live.\nHer sister married in the same commune six years later.\n\nNo birth date: the record gives her none, not even an age, so this record has none either.\n\n`sup`: an indexed registration. The act's own words have not been read — only the\ntranscription and the register page it sits on.\n\nFRONTIER: her own birth act, and any children of the van der Varent marriage."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"morree","name":"Anna Francisca Morree","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Morree","family":"morree","branch":"Devriendt","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"francl_s","name":"Franciscus Leopoldus Smessaert"}],"source":"Marriage act — Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert × Anna Francisca Morbeé, Brugge, 16 August 1851","note":"STRONG LEAD, NOT GRAFTED (July 2026) — see [[francl_s]] for the whole of it. A Brugge\nmarriage act of 1851 gives an Anna Francisca **Morbeé**, daughter of Petrus Josephus Morbeé\nand Joanna De Clerck, marrying a Franciscus Léopoldus Smessaert. The forenames and the\nhusband match; the surname does not.\n\nMorree and Morbeé are a plausible pair to confuse in a nineteenth-century hand — the double\nr and the rb are near-identical in cursive — and this record's spelling comes from a member\ntree, not from an act. That makes the act the better authority in principle, but \"in\nprinciple\" is not evidence, so nothing is changed here. Her son's 1857 Oostende birth act\nwould settle which spelling the registrar used."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"mtheresia_vandenbroeck","name":"Maria Theresia Van den Broeck","dates":"","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van den Broeck","family":"vandenbroeck","died":"","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"desiderius_dk","name":"Desiderius De Keyser"}],"source":"Édouard Dekeyser's 1946 Oostende remarriage act (akte nr. 81); FamilySearch","note":"Source detail: Oostende marriage act nr. 81, 9 May 1946 (FamilySearch, Belgium West Flanders Civil Registration 1582-1950 — image read directly), naming her as mother of Eduardus De Keyser\n\nMOTHER of Édouard Dekeyser. Named in Édouard's 1946 remarriage act as his mother, 'overleden' (deceased) by then. Van den Broeck is a Waasland / Hamme (Oost-Vlaanderen) name, consistent with the family's Hamme origin. Frontier: her dates/parents, in the Hamme (O.-Vl.) registers."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"mtstephanie_t","name":"Marie Thérèse Stéphanie Thumas","dates":"b. Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"sup","surname":"Thumas","family":"thumas","sex":"f","born":"Grez-Doiceau","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"georges2_t","mother":"joostens","source":"The children of Georges Thumas x Marie Catherine Joostens at Grez-Doiceau, 1835-1868","note":"Eldest known child of [[georges2_t]] and [[joostens]], and an elder sister of\n[[georges_cj]]. Her birth was declared at Grez-Doiceau on **11 August 1835** (S25), under six\nmonths after her parents married there on 17 February 1835.\n\n`raw` rather than a date because the index gives the **declaration**, not the birth.\n\n`sup`: an index row, no register image read. `sex` is recorded from the forenames *only*\nbecause the register itself declines them in the feminine and the index marks the row so —\nnot inferred from how the name reads.\n\nFRONTIER: her birth act, and whether she lived to marry. Nothing is known of her after 1835."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"nadia","name":"Nadia Bundervoet","dates":"","confidence":"fam","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"f","line":"bundervoet","father":"marcel_b","mother":"rosette"});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"nicolas_verbrugghe","name":"Nicolas Verbrugghe","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verbrugghe","family":"verbrugghe","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"name":"(wife unrecorded)"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Father of Joanna (Janneken) Verbrugghe (~1655–1704), and so a direct ancestor through\nher son Joannes Bundervoet (~1682).\n\nNamed as her father in the paulderidder tree's ancestry chart; the tree gives him no\ndates at all and no wife, which is why this record carries none either. Joanna's\nrecord previously said her parents were \"not recorded here\" — they were, and this\ncorrects that.\n\nFRONTIER: everything about him. Evergem parish registers for a Verbrugghe–? marriage\nin the 1640s–50s would be the first place to look, since a daughter born ~1655 puts\nthe marriage a little before it."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"nicolas_willaert","name":"Nicolas Willaert","dates":"~1595 – 1659","confidence":"sup","surname":"Willaert","family":"willaert","born":"~1595","order":"1595","died":"1659","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"catharina_vanmassenhove","name":"Catharina Van Massenhove"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"FRONTIER above — father of Joanna Willaert (1631 Torhout). Born ~1595."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"nn_vandenberghe","name":"NN Vandenberghe","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandenberghe","family":"vandenberghe","sex":"f","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"judocus_sabbe_1475","name":"Judocus (Joos) Sabbe"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Wife of [[judocus_sabbe_1475]] (~1475–1534) and, on that reading, the mother of\n[[petrus_sabbe_1504]] — though isavdw states the marriage and not the maternity, so\nthe parent link is deliberately not made here.\n\nHer given name is not recorded; only the family name survives. Written the same way\nas [[elisabeth_nn]], the opposite case — a given name and no surname. A name half\nknown is recorded half, never completed.\n\nNo relation to [[judoca_vandenberghe]] is established: that is a different\nVandenberghe, a century later and in a different parish. Same surname is not a link."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"nn_vyveraert","name":"NN Vyveraert","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vyveraert","family":"vyveraert","sex":"f","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"petrus_bundervoet1560","name":"Petrus Bundervoet"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"Wife of [[petrus_bundervoet1560]], the earliest recorded ancestor of the Bundervoet\nline. Her given name is not recorded — only the family name — so she is written the\nway [[nn_vandenberghe]] is, and for the same reason.\n\nHis record says he married twice; this is the only wife either tree names, and\nwhich of the two marriages it was is not stated. Whether [[livinus_bundervoet]] is\nher son or the other wife's is therefore open, and the maternity is deliberately not\nrecorded. FRONTIER — an Evergem marriage act naming her."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"noel_t","name":"Marie Catherine Noël","dates":"19 Jan 1751 Grez-Doiceau – 2 Aug 1812 Grez-Doiceau","confidence":"doc","surname":"Noël","family":"noel","born":"19 Jan 1751 Grez-Doiceau","order":"1751-01-19","died":"2 Aug 1812 Grez-Doiceau","occupation":"bierverkoopster (beer seller)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","spouses":[{"id":"georges1_t","name":"Georges Thumas","detail":"m. Grez-Doiceau, 3 Jan 1771"}],"source":"Death act nr. 58 — George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808 (read on AGATHA); Death act of George Thumas, Grez-Doiceau, 20 November 1808; Geneanet","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a wife. Her husband's death act (Grez-Doiceau, 20 November\n1808) names his wife as *Marie Catherine Noël*, which puts the marriage on a civil act\nrather than on a tree. She outlived him by nearly four years.\n\nMarried the carpenter Georges Thumas at Grez-Doiceau in 1771; worked as a beer seller. Daughter of Jean Baptiste Noël × Marie Josephe Derossart.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named as the partner of the deceased in her husband's 1808\nGrez-Doiceau death act — written **Marie Catherine Noé** there, not Noël. The act puts the\nmarriage beyond the trees; the spelling is recorded as a variant rather than adopted, since\nher own record and this tree's other sources use Noël."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"octavia_schal","name":"Octavia Maria Schalandrijn","dates":"b. 30 Apr 1886 Bredene","confidence":"doc","surname":"Schalandrijn","family":"schalandrijn","born":"30 Apr 1886 Bredene","order":"1886-04-30","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"van-iseghem","father":"ludovicus_schal","mother":"mathilde_standaert","spouses":[{"id":"eugenius_dv","name":"Eugenius Alphonsius Devriendt","detail":"m. Oostende, 10 Nov 1906"}],"source":"gverdievel (Guy Verdievel); Marriage act nr. 258 — Eugenius Alphonsius Devriendt × Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Oostende, 10 November 1906; Birth act nr. 116 — Octavia Maria Schalandrijn, Bredene, certificate dated 2 May 1886","note":"Born in the coastal village of Bredene; mother of Adrienne Devriendt.\n\nCORRECTED (2026-07-26): birth date corrected from 1886-05-02 to 1886-04-30. The date\nheld here was the certificate/registration date, not the birth date. The Bredene birth\nact itself (nr. 116, S21), read as an image, says she was born \"eergisteren de\ndertigsten April\" (the day before yesterday, the thirtieth of April) against an act\ndate of 2 May 1886; the 1906 marriage act (nr. 258, S20), read separately, independently\ngives the same 30 April date. See docs/research-log.md §48 for the retraction (§46\ncovers a source-id collision from the same pass).\n\nGRAFTED (2026-07-26): parents identified from the same 1906 Oostende marriage act,\nread as an image — father Ludovicus Schalandryn (werkman, resident at Oostende), mother\nMathilde Standaert (already deceased by 1906). See [[ludovicus_schal]] and\n[[mathilde_standaert]] for what the acts do and do not support about them beyond this."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"oliverius_stroobandt","name":"Oliverius Stroobandt","dates":"d. 1660–1670","confidence":"sup","surname":"Stroobandt","family":"stroobandt","died":"1660–1670","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"judoca_vanhecke","name":"Judoca Van Hecke"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"FRONTIER above — top of the documented Stroobandt surname line (born ~1590s). His own parents not recorded."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"paula_v","name":"Paula Mathilde Vanstechelman","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vanstechelman","family":"vanstechelman","sex":"f","branch":"Vanstechelman","line":"vanstechelman","father":"petrusjacobus_v","mother":"clementia_w","spouses":[{"id":"alberic_delrue","name":"Alberic Luciaan Delrue","detail":"m. Oostende, 11 May 1924"}],"source":"België, West-Vlaanderen, burgerlijke stand, 1582-1950","note":"Sister of [[augusta]], named in her own Oostende marriage registration of 11 May 1924, which\ngives her parents as Petrus Jacobus and Clemence Wagebaert — the mother's name shortened\nthere, as it is in several of these acts — and her husband as Alberic Luciaan Delrue.\n\nNo dates of her own yet; the act is indexed under the marriage. FRONTIER: her birth act, and\nthe marriage act read rather than indexed."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"paulus_lampsins","name":"Paulus Lampsins","dates":"~1600 – 1659","confidence":"sup","surname":"Lampsins","family":"lampsins","born":"~1600","order":"1600","died":"1659","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"clara_lampsins","name":"Clara Lampsins"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"FRONTIER above — father of Maria Lampsins (1637 Lichtervelde). NOTE: this is the ordinary Lichtervelde Lampsins family, distinct from the noble 'Dame van Zwevezele' Lampsins line (a namesake earlier avoided)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"peremans","name":"Joanna Catharina Jacoba Peremans","dates":"1824 Zaventem – 1907","confidence":"doc","surname":"Peremans","family":"peremans","born":"1824 Zaventem","order":"1824","died":"1907","occupation":"huishoudster (housekeeper)","branch":"Thumas","line":"thumas","father":"egidius_peremans","mother":"joanna_verelst","spouses":[{"id":"guilielmus_bossin","name":"Guilielmus Bossin","detail":"m. Zaventem, 24 Feb 1846"}],"source":"Marriage banns of Cornelius Peremans, Zaventem, 21 April 1844; Marriage of Petrus van der Varent x Maria Josephina Peremans, Zaventem, 5 November 1840; Zaventem marriage act nr. 1, 24 February 1846 — Bossin × Peremans; Kraainem marriage act nr. 2, 20 June 1872 — Thumas × Bossin (read on AGATHA); Marriage act — Georges Carolus Josephus Thumas × Antonia Bossin, Kraainem, 20 June 1872","note":"CORROBORATED (July 2026) as a mother, by her daughter's Kraainem marriage act of\n20 June 1872, which names the bride's parents as Guilielmus Bossin and *Anna* Catharina\nPeremans. The act's forenames are shorter than the ones this record carries — Anna\nCatharina against Joanna Catharina Jacoba — which is ordinary for a civil act quoting a\nparent, but it is a difference, and it is recorded rather than smoothed over.\n\nACT READ (July 2026): named in her daughter's 1872 marriage act as *huishoudster*, living\nat Kraainem. The act calls her Anna Catharina; this record calls her Joanna Catharina\nJacoba. Both stand.\n\nACT READ (2026-07-26): her own marriage act — Zaventem nr. 1, 24 February 1846 (S19),\nread as an image. It **settles the forename dispute above in this record's favour**: the\nact that married her calls her *Joanna Catharina Jacoba Peremans*, in full, which is what\nthis tree held. The shorter *Anna Catharina* of her daughter's 1872 act was the act\nquoting a parent from memory, and it is now the outlier rather than a rival reading.\n\nShe was **born at Zaventem** and was **21**, which confirms the 1824 from a civil act and\nmatches her husband year for year. Her occupation at marriage was *arbeidster*.\n\nThe act names her parents [[egidius_peremans]] and [[joanna_verelst]], both already dead\n— he at Zaventem on 6 March 1837, she at Zaventem on 19 December 1843 — so she married at\ntwenty-one an orphan on both sides. And it records something registers rarely bother with:\nshe declared, with her witnesses, that **she had never known her grandparents nor where\nthey died**. That is a documented dead end, not a gap to keep searching by name.\n\nFRONTIER — three probable siblings, named and not grafted (2026-07-26). FamilySearch's index\nof the Brabant civil registration returns, for *Egidius Peremans*, several rows giving his\nspouse as **Joanna Theresia ver Elst** and a child other than her: **Maria Josephina\nPeremans**, **Joannes Athanasius Peremans**, and a **Cornelius Peremans** whose mother is given\nin the shorter form *Theresia Verelst*.\n\nThe parent pair matches [[egidius_peremans]] and [[joanna_verelst]] exactly, and *Athanasius*\nis rare enough to be worth something on its own. They are still not grafted, for a specific\nreason: **none of those rows carries an event date or a place.** Rule 1 wants two independent\nidentifiers with one of them anchored, and a parent pair with no commune and no year is not\nanchored. The same search, narrowed by parent, then drifted to a quite different family of\nPeremans in Antwerp — FamilySearch's parent filters are advisory, which this log has recorded\nbefore — so the rows need opening one by one before any of them becomes a person here.\n\nONE OPENED (2026-07-26), and it anchored. **Maria Josephina** married *Petrús van der Varent*\non **5 November 1840** — and the place, which the indexed record does not carry, comes from the\ntitle of the volume the page sits in: ***Zaventem. Huwelijksakten 1840***. Zaventem is where\nthis record's father died, where her mother died, and where she herself was born and married.\nPlace plus an exact parent pair is two identifiers with one anchored, so [[mjosephina_peremans]]\nis now in the tree as her sister, with a husband and his parents.\n\nTWO OPENED (2026-07-26), both anchored the same way. **[[cornelius_peremans]]** had his\nmarriage banns published at **Zaventem on 21 April 1844** (S30) — four months after his mother\ndied and seven years after his father — with the parent pair given in the short form *Egidius\nPeremans × Theresia Verelst*. His bride is deliberately not recorded: the index lists three\nmore people in that document and states the role of none of them.\n\n*Joannes Athanasius* is the one row still unopened. The same move should settle him.\n\n**And the 1840 act points at what §47 could not reach.** [[egidius_peremans]] was already dead\nin November 1840, so marrying his daughter required an extract of his death act, bound into\nthat volume as a *huwelijksbijlage* — the exact mechanism that produced [[S23]]. Vlaams-Brabant\nindexes no death acts at all, which makes the annexes to this 1840 marriage the best route to\nhis 6 March 1837 act, and they are one volume away."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petronella_b1754","name":"Petronella Bundervoet","dates":"1754 – 1794","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","sex":"f","born":"1754","order":"1754","died":"1794","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"petrus_b1727","mother":"marie_anna_dedeckere","source":"paulderidder","note":"One of the eight children of [[petrus_b1727]] and [[marie_anna_dedeckere]]. Their father was\nthe younger brother of [[christoffel]], through whom this tree's line runs, so these eight are\nfirst cousins of [[philippus]]'s generation — blood relatives of Renée and Léon under\nobjective 2.\n\nRecorded from the paulderidder tree's list of the couple's children, which gives the years\nabove and nothing further. No act has been read for Petronella: a birth act at Evergem\nor Assenede would give the day and the parents in the register's own words."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petronella_v","name":"Petronella Verniers","dates":"26 Sep 1661 Destelbergen – 16 Feb 1709 Destelbergen","confidence":"sup","surname":"Verniers","family":"verniers","born":"26 Sep 1661 Destelbergen","order":"1661-09-26","died":"16 Feb 1709 Destelbergen","branch":"Paelinck","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"ludovicus_p","name":"Ludovicus Paelinck","detail":"m. Lochristi, Feb 1681"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"Lived her whole documented life in Destelbergen; wife of Ludovicus Paelinck and mother of Adrianus (1690)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petronilla_vk","name":"Petronilla Carolina Van Kerckhove","dates":"14 Mar 1712 Kalken – 17 Mar 1791 Destelbergen","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Kerckhove","family":"vankerckhove","born":"14 Mar 1712 Kalken","order":"1712-03-14","died":"17 Mar 1791 Destelbergen","branch":"Paelinck","line":"paelinck","spouses":[{"id":"livinus2_p","name":"Livinus Paelinck","detail":"m. Kalken, 7 Nov 1739"}],"source":"stefpaelinck (Stef Paelinck)","note":"From Kalken; married there in 1739 and later died in Destelbergen. Mother of Apolonius (1748)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_b1727","name":"Petrus (Pieter) Bundervoet","dates":"~1727 Evergem – 1777","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"~1727 Evergem","order":"1727","died":"1777","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"joannes_b","mother":"livina_stockman","spouses":[{"id":"marie_anna_dedeckere","name":"Marie Anna de Deckere","detail":"m. ~1750"}],"source":"paulderidder","note":"Younger son of Joannes Bundervoet (~1682–1760) and Livina Stockman, and the brother of\nChristoffel (1709–1786) through whom our line descends. He existed in this tree only as\nthe string \"Pieter (1727)\" inside his father's note; every person referenced anywhere is\nsupposed to have their own record, and now he does.\n\nThe death is recorded as a burial, not a death: paulderidder gives \"deceased, aged about\n50\" with a burial at Assenede on 13 December 1777, and no date of death. The year is\nsafe, the day is the burial's, and the two are kept apart rather than collapsed into a\ndeath date the source never gave. Assenede, a little north of Evergem, is also the first\nsign of this branch moving off the home parish.\n\nHIS FAMILY IS NOW IN THE TREE — his wife [[marie_anna_dedeckere]] and all eight children. From\npaulderidder: married about 1750 to Marie Anna de Deckere (~1731–1809), with Joannis\n(1751), Livinus (1752), Petronella (1754–1794), Christophorus (1755), Joannis Baptista\n(1757), Livina Maria (1760–1831), Joanna (1761–1825) and Coleta (1766–1807). They are\nblood relatives of Renée and Léon — a great-uncle's whole household — and belong in the\ntree under objective 2. They are listed here rather than grafted because this pass took\nthe direct ancestors first, as the charter's priority requires.\n\nA second document sits on his paulderidder profile, captioned \"Petrus Bundervoet Akte\nvan teraardebestelling\" — a burial act. Not yet retrieved."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_blomme","name":"Petrus Blomme","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Blomme","family":"blomme","sex":"m","branch":"DeKeyser","line":"de-keyser","spouses":[{"id":"louise_bocklandt","name":"Louise Marie Bocklandt"}],"source":"Memorial-card record — Louisa-Maria Bocklandt, d. Oostende 15 July 1946","note":"Second husband of [[louise_bocklandt]], who had divorced [[edouard_dk]] around 1923.\nThe Familiekunde Westkust memorial-card record ([[S17]]) names him as her partner at\nher death on 15 July 1946 — she died a Blomme. The card names him and nothing more.\n\nNo marriage date, so none is recorded. FRONTIER — the Bocklandt–Blomme marriage act.\nIt is post-1923 Oostende, so it sits at the Stadsarchief rather than in AGATHA.\n\nHe is a step-relation, not blood: no line of descent here runs through him."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_bundervoet1560","name":"Petrus Bundervoet","dates":"1560 – ~1605","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"1560","order":"1560","died":"~1605","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","spouses":[{"id":"nn_vyveraert","name":"NN Vyveraert"}],"source":"paulderidder; glorieuxp","note":"The earliest documented ancestor of the Bundervoet line (Evergem, ~1560); married twice and was the father of Livinus.\n\nCORRECTION (July 2026) to the note recorded a pass earlier. The full-text find was written\nup from search snippets as \"a Catherine Bundervoet widowed at Meirelbeke in 1587\" and a fief\nchain of 1687-1700. Reading the actual page ([[bundervoet-fiefs-alost-1687-1701]]) shows the\nsnippets had merged two adjacent entries: the Meirelbeke 1587 one belongs to the surname VAN\nDEN BUNDERE, not Bundervoet.\n\nWhat the page does show is a Bundervoet family at **Saint-Pierre-Alost**, holding fiefs from\n**1687 to 1701** — Catherine as widow and guardian in 1687, then Liévin son of François and\nLiévin son of Pasquier in 1700, and Pasquier son of Liévin in 1701. Descent stated, in the\nright century, some 30 km from Evergem. A lead for objective 3, and still not a link."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_debaecke","name":"Petrus De Baecke","dates":"b. ~1600","confidence":"sup","surname":"De Baecke","family":"debaecke","born":"~1600","order":"1600","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"margaretha_wybau","name":"Margaretha Wybau"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"FRONTIER above — father of Adrianus De Baecke (1630). Dates and parents not recorded."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_degrande","name":"Petrus De Grande","dates":"1697 – 1765","confidence":"sup","surname":"De Grande","family":"degrande","born":"1697","order":"1697","died":"1765","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"egidius_degrande","mother":"joanna_wallays","spouses":[{"id":"adriana_sabbe","name":"Adriana Theresia Sabbe"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Father of Michael De Grande (1726)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_devos","name":"Petrus Jacobus Franciscus Devos","dates":"","confidence":"sup","surname":"Devos","family":"devos","branch":"Devriendt","line":"devriendt","spouses":[{"id":"loncke","name":"Charlotte Maria Loncke"}]});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_f","name":"Petrus Franciscus Bundervoet","dates":"19 Mar 1879 Evergem – 21 Jul 1943 Oostende","confidence":"sup","surname":"Bundervoet","family":"bundervoet","born":"19 Mar 1879 Evergem","order":"1879-03-19","died":"21 Jul 1943 Oostende","occupation":"werkman / meestergast","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bundervoet","father":"bernardus","mother":"goethals","spouses":[{"id":"augusta","name":"Augusta Vanstechelman"}],"source":"Doodsprentjes.be memorial card — Pieter Franciscus Bundervoet, d. Oostende 21 July 1943; Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust memorial card — Pieter-Franciscus Bundervoet, d. Oostende 21 July 1943; Geneanet","note":"The FIRST of the Bundervoet line to leave Evergem for the coast: born in Evergem, he settled in Oostende, where all his children were born from 1905 onward. Married Augusta Vanstechelman (the Bundervoet–Vanstechelman junction). FRONTIER (MyHeritage, July 2026): two independent Bundervoet family trees on MyHeritage — one run by Lucien Bundervoet, one by Johny Henricus Bundervoet, both in Belgium — agree that he and Augusta had SIX children, not the one recorded here: Alphons Bernardus Cyprianus, Emilius Josephus, Achilles, Henricus Eduardus, Irena Augusta and Camillus Edmundus. The same trees give him at least four siblings, one named Maria Bundervoet. His own birth and death match ours exactly (19 Mar 1879 Evergem, 21 Jul 1943), which is what makes the match credible. NOT GRAFTED: member trees are not records and no dates for the children were readable, so the five siblings need their Oostende birth acts (1905 onward) before they go in.\n\nCORROBORATED (July 2026), and by two archives that do not share a source. Doodsprentjes.be\nand Familiekunde Vlaanderen Westkust each hold a memorial-card record for him, and both\ngive birth 19 March 1879 at Evergem, death 21 July 1943 at Oostende, and a Vanstechelman\npartner — the Familiekunde one naming her in full as Augusta. Four identifiers agreeing\nacross two independent collections, where before this record rested on a Geneanet tree.\n\nConfidence stays `sup` rather than rising to `doc`: these are transcriptions of memorial\ncards. The Doodsprentjes scan is behind a session — the record's image URL returns the\nsite's search page, not the card — so no image has been read here. Reading it, or the\nOostende 1943 civil death act, is what would make this `doc`."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_jos_keirsebilck","name":"Petrus Josephus Keirsebilck","dates":"13 Oct 1764 Oostkamp – 20 May 1817 Oostkamp","confidence":"sup","surname":"Keirsebilck","family":"keirsebilck","born":"13 Oct 1764 Oostkamp","order":"1764-10-13","died":"20 May 1817 Oostkamp","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"joannes_keirsebilck_1728","mother":"maria_c_declerck","spouses":[{"id":"anna_fr_degrande","name":"Anna Francisca De Grande","detail":"m. Oostkamp, 4 Oct 1785"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Father of Joanna Keirsebilck (1791). Parents Joannes Keirsebilck (1728-1781) x Maria Catharina De Clerck (1727-1768)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_sabbe","name":"Petrus Sabbe","dates":"d. 31 Dec 1652 Oostkamp (Ruddervoorde)","confidence":"sup","surname":"Sabbe","family":"sabbe","died":"31 Dec 1652 Oostkamp (Ruddervoorde)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"willem_sabbe_y","mother":"clara_vandeputte","spouses":[{"id":"judoca_vandenberghe","name":"Judoca Vandenberghe","detail":"m. Oostkamp (Ruddervoorde), 11 Jun 1616"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Source detail: Geneanet isavdw (Rijksarchief aktes; Sosa 6760)\n\nAlso 'Schabbe'. Married Judoca Vandenberghe 1616; nine children incl. Simon Sabbe (1627). Witness at the wedding was his uncle Michiel Sabbe (b.1557). Parents Willem Sabbe x Clara Vande Putte. The Sabbe line runs back to Judocus 'Joos' Sabbe (~1475) around Harelbeke."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_sabbe_1504","name":"Petrus Sabbe","dates":"1504 Zwevegem – 1557","confidence":"sup","surname":"Sabbe","family":"sabbe","born":"1504 Zwevegem","order":"1504","died":"1557","occupation":"landbouwer (farmer)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"judocus_sabbe_1475","spouses":[{"name":"(wife unrecorded)"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Born 1504 in Zwevegem (reign of Charles V), a farmer. Father of Willem Sabbe (~1530). Son of Judocus 'Joos' Sabbe (~1475), grandson of Gillis Sabbe (~1440)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_vandewalle","name":"Petrus Vandewalle","dates":"d. 1658","confidence":"sup","surname":"Vandewalle","family":"vandewalle","died":"1658","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"simon_vandewalle_1565","mother":"christina_desangere","spouses":[{"id":"francisca_vanhoutte","name":"Francisca Van Houtte","kind":"partnership","detail":"partner"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"Father of Carolus Vandewalle (1638, born out of wedlock to Francisca Van Houtte). Son of Simon Vandewalle, the sexton of Oostkamp."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_vannieuwenhuyse","name":"Petrus Van Nieuwenhuyse","dates":"7 Mar 1649 Oostkamp – 1701","confidence":"doc","surname":"Van Nieuwenhuyse","family":"vannieuwenhuyse","born":"7 Mar 1649 Oostkamp","order":"1649-03-07","died":"1701","occupation":"schepen van Oostkamp (alderman)","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","father":"marinus_vannieuwenhuyse","mother":"cornelia_govaert","spouses":[{"id":"jacoba_monballiu","name":"Jacoba Monballiu","detail":"m. Oostkamp, 23 Jul 1673"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links; Rijksarchief AGATHA — Belgian State Archives search robot","note":"Source detail: Geneanet isavdw; birth act agatha.arch.be scan 513_9000_000_00774 (Sosa 3382)\n\nFather of Anna Van Nieuwenhuyse (1676). Served as a schepen (alderman/magistrate) of Oostkamp. Parents Marinus Van Nieuwenhuyse (~1620-1666) x Cornelia Govaert (~1625-1653)."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_vanrenterghem","name":"Petrus Van Renterghem","dates":"~1500 – before 1530","confidence":"sup","surname":"Van Renterghem","family":"vanrenterghem","born":"~1500","order":"1500","died":"before 1530","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"name":"(wife unrecorded)"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"DEEPEST-TIER ANCESTOR — born ~1500, Oostkamp area. Father of Guillielmus Van Renterghem (~1530). Top of this line; no parents recorded."});
FamilyTree.person({"id":"petrus_wittenheyns","name":"Petrus Wittenheyns","dates":"~1500 – before 1575","confidence":"sup","surname":"Wittenheyns","family":"wittenheyns","born":"~1500","order":"1500","died":"before 1575","branch":"Bundervoet","line":"bostyn-cappaert","spouses":[{"id":"judoca_tjonck","name":"Judoca 't Jonck"}],"source":"isavdw — Rijksarchief-sourced, with scan links","note":"DEEPEST-TIER ANCESTOR — born ~1500, Oostkamp. Father of Barbara Wittenheyns (~1535). The Wittenheyns of Oostkamp appear on two independent lines of ours (also\n[[mattheus_wittenheyns]] ~1500, via the Vandewalle line); whether Petrus and Mattheus\nare brothers is not established. No parents recorded.\n\nCHECKED AND REJECTED (July 2026) — the duplicate detector flags Petrus and Mattheus as\npossibly one person, on a rare surname plus a birth year of about 1500. They are not.\nFour things separate them, and none is a spelling difference:\n\n- different given names — Mattheus and Petrus are not variants of one another;\n- different wives — Judoca 't Jonck here, Maria De Ruwe there;\n- different deaths — before 1575 here, about 1546 at Oostkamp there;\n- different children — Barbara (~1535) here; Mattheus's children are named with him in\n  the 1547 Bruges orphan register.\n\nTwo men of one uncommon surname, born about the same time in the same parish, is what a\npair of brothers or cousins looks like. The warning is expected to keep firing, because\nit is derived from surname and year alone; this note is the answer to it."});
